-## #3915 - D3: The face names are held in memory only in this PR
+## #4212 - D3: The face names are held in memory only in this PR
 
 **Decided.** A model imported from a `.sc` design carries `schema::SourceFaces { rev, len, record }`, written and read only through `source_faces::{set, of}`. It is not saved: the project file does not change, and a reopened project has no names. `of` gives the record only at the revision and facet count it was landed with, and only when its ranges tile the facets (the `SolidRanges` guard, #917). `ImportModel` lands it. `UpdateModel::with_source_faces` states it, and the update trades it on undo; an update that does not state it drops it, so `RepairModel` (through `keeping_fidelity`, which does not keep it), an update from a file that is not `.sc`, and the vise, accessory and plate rebuilds drop the names. `DeleteEntity` puts it back on undo. The window's re-import, the script and MCP `import_model`, and the fixture re-import state it.
 

From 35387c90ebb2fd9045a48db59c012b609281cb38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Britten <11667518+marcbritten@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:51:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] feat(mcp): import_model answers an update with its
 feature changes

When import_model updates a model that was there before the call, the
answer gets the optional key `changes`: for the faces, the welded faces
and the edge chains, the carried, added and missing id counts, and the
window's phrase (`FeatureChanges::describe`). The diff is
`revision::changes`, the one `UpdateModel::changes` gives the window.
A first import has no `changes`.

The hook in mcp/tools.rs is four lines. The logic is in the new
mcp/reimport_changes.rs. It keeps each model's facets (Arc) and revision
before the call, then selects the model by the answer's own `model`
name, so script/api.rs (which #4212 and #4213 change) is not touched.

Tests: crates/app/tests/mcp/reimport_changes.rs.
Decision entries: this PR's file in docs/decisions/.

Built and tested on the earlier base 773736856 (the PR body lists the
runs). Rebased onto a721fd4dc without a local build; the maintainer's
runners test it.

